A number of dishes are traditionally eaten on New Year's Day in Japan;
each has special symbolic meaning (e.g. good health in the upcoming
year). They seem like good candidates for special holiday food.

Since tracing uses `debugprint`'s to collect trace data, the opcode should be treated as `write`. This PR makes this change, annotating the funcs in ArbOS that produce debug info & fixing an induced optimizer bug among the novel scenarios generated.

Additionally, this PR
- Introduces & statically enforces the `throw` keyword for funcs that may raise an explicit error
- Adds the `safe` keyword for funcs that have been rigorously audited for safety
- Sprinkles these keywords throughout ArbOS and the standard libraries

```rs
public view write throw func safeSetGlobalAccountStore(acctStore: AccountStore) {
    if ! evmCallStack_isEmpty() {
        asm(669) { debugprint };
        error;
    }
}

